  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the supplied task and tooling guidance, then build and verify the application end to end in the workspace. I’ll preserve `TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md`, use only local/synthetic data, and record checks and any limitations in the project documentation.",
    "I’m choosing a dependency-free Python stack: `http.server` with SQLite in WAL mode, a vanilla browser client, and route-level integration/load scripts. This keeps startup reproducible and lets transaction, idempotency, and persistence behavior be exercised against the real HTTP surface.",
    "The initial implementation is in place: SQLite schema/seed data, tenant-scoped sessions, atomic state transitions, durable idempotency/audit records, and the responsive workflow UI. I’m moving into route-level verification now; any defects found in those checks will be fixed before documenting results.",
    "The HTTP integration suite now passes 13 areas, including atomic multi-line failure, concurrent reservations, concurrent identical retries, stale versions, returns, tenant isolation, pagination, and restart durability. I’m checking the actual browser workflow next, then I’ll add the repeatable performance exercise and finalize documentation with only measured results.",
    "The browser check passed against the real UI at a 390px viewport: login, multi-line order creation, reserve/ship/full return, audit rendering, logout, viewer control hiding, and zero console errors. The local workload also completed with zero errors; I’m doing a final clean verification pass and reviewing edge-case semantics before handoff.",
    "I found and corrected one UI consistency issue during review: the audit view now refetches from the beginning whenever it is opened, so post-mutation audit state cannot remain stale. I also tightened cursor tenant binding and rejected values outside SQLite’s integer range; the route suite still passes.",
    "All requested artifacts are now present with no temporary data left in the workspace. The final review confirms tenant-scoped reads/writes, durable idempotency, safe DOM rendering, executable startup scripts, actual route tests, browser evidence, and the documented benchmark/limitations. I’m running one last syntax/setup/integration check before handing it over.",
    "Completed DepotFlow with:\n\n- SQLite-backed multi-tenant backend and durable idempotency/audit state\n- Atomic reservations, shipping, cancellation, returns, version checks, and tenant isolation\n- Responsive frontend with viewer read-only behavior and required `data-testid` markers\n- Integration tests, Playwright browser check, and repeatable load test\n- Executable [run.sh](<CELL>/workspace/run.sh)\n- Documentation in [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md) and [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md)\n\nVerification passed:\n\n- 13 integration areas, including concurrency and restart durability\n- Browser workflow: 3 inventory rows, 4 audit events, no viewer mutation controls, no mobile overflow, zero console errors\n- Load test: 0 errors; 2,655 read req/s and 1,830 write req/s at 4-way concurrency\n\n`TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md` were preserved."
  ],
